)}>a</button>
```

Yes it's already possible, but not really the recommended way for a simple handler.
I wouldn't expect a migration tool to generate `on:action` in order to handle events

So in the previous example the multiple `on:click` would generate something like this :
```svelte
<button 
    on:addEventListener={['click', (eve) => console.log(eve)]}
    on:addEventListener={['click', (eve) => console.log(eve)]}
    on:addEventListener={['click', (event) => {
        event.preventDefault();
        stuff.?();
    }]}
